From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 01:42:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Widen license-files to cover the bundled FFTW licence

`license-files = ["LICENSE.txt"]` is a PEP 639 list, so it has no
`LICEN[CS]E*` auto-discovery glob behind it: a `LICENSE.fftw` dropped at
the project root to cover the libfftw3* libraries `auditwheel repair`
vendors into pyfftw.libs/ is silently ignored. Widening the entry to
`LICENSE*` still matches LICENSE.txt on its own (so the sdist is
unaffected) and picks up the staged FFTW notice in the wheel build.

Upstream's own Linux wheels carry the same gap: they vendor libfftw3,
libfftw3f, libfftw3l and their _omp variants (GPL-2.0-or-later) but ship
only LICENSE.txt in dist-info/licenses.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not submitted from this automated port run; needs a pull request against pyFFTW/pyFFTW]
---
 pyproject.toml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/pyproject.toml b/pyproject.toml
index 8621d94..fe4d3c5 100644
--- a/pyproject.toml
+++ b/pyproject.toml
@@ -28,7 +28,7 @@ dependencies = [
 ]
 readme = "README.md"
 license = "BSD-3-Clause"
-license-files = ["LICENSE.txt"]
+license-files = ["LICENSE*"]
 classifiers = [
     "Development Status :: 5 - Production/Stable",
     "Intended Audience :: Developers",
-- 
2.43.0

